    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35975" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνορούω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leap in</i> or <i>upon,</i> usu. of an assault, c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρωσὶ . . ἐνόρουσεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.783
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς δὲ λέων . . αἴγεσιν ἢ ὀΐεσσι .
					. ἐνορούσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.486
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δ᾽ Ἀγαμέμνων πρῶτος ὄρουσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.217
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ ἀνέδην ἐνοροῦον</span>
			prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Cord.</u>
				2
			</span></i>; of fish, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήεσσιν ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					2.516
				</span></i>
			.</div>
